config VAPOROS_TOYBOX
	tristate "toybox -- vendored multicall, 13 applets so far (docs/vaporshell.md)"
	default n
	---help---
		Vendored toybox (codeberg.org/landley/toybox), patched for
		NuttX portability, built as a single multicall "tbx"
		program. vaporshell spawns it with argv[0] set to whichever
		applet name was typed (posix_spawnp("tbx", ..., argv)),
		the same way a real Unix symlink-based multicall install
		would work, just resolved by vaporshell's own table instead
		of the filesystem.

		Registered as "tbx". vaporshell/NuttX's own Application.mk
		renames this program's real entry point to <PROGNAME>_main
		-- and toybox's own main.c unconditionally calls an
		internal multiplexer function that ALSO needs to be named
		exactly "toybox_main" (wired to generated/newtoys.h's own
		hardcoded "toybox" table entry via macro token-pasting, not
		something a plain rename can dodge). Rather than fight that,
		this build's real entry point is vapor_entry.c, not
		toybox's own main.c -- it calls toybox's public toy_exec()
		directly instead of going through toybox's own main()/
		toybox_main() dispatcher at all, so PROGNAME never has to
		match anything toybox's own generated tables hardcode. Run
		applets as `tbx true`, `tbx echo hi`, etc.

		Batch 2: added cat, mkdir, rmdir, touch, printf, rm.
		Batch 3: added ls, cp, mv (mv_main lives in cp.c, no
		separate mv.c upstream). One real NuttX-specific gap found
		and fixed: cp's own cp_xattr() unconditionally calls
		xattr_get/set/list, which are genuinely absent on NuttX
		(same as lib/portability.c's own existing treatment) --
		only reachable via explicit --preserve=xattr/all, not plain
		-p/-a, so given an honest non-fatal warning instead of
		either erroring the whole copy or silently pretending it
		worked. Still not the full ~218-command set. See the
		Makefile in this directory for what expanding scope
		actually requires (mainly:
		regenerating generated/*.h on a host toybox checkout).

if VAPOROS_TOYBOX

config VAPOROS_TOYBOX_PROGNAME
	string "Program name"
	default "tbx"

config VAPOROS_TOYBOX_PRIORITY
	int "priority"
	default 100

config VAPOROS_TOYBOX_STACKSIZE
	int "stack size"
	default DEFAULT_TASK_STACKSIZE

endif
